15. Navarasa Engagement Fix

The Navarasa engine was expanded to recognize engagement, curiosity, excitement, and exploratory interaction.
Examples included:
- “tell me more”
- “keep going”
- “I want to understand”
- “I want to know”
- “this matters to me”
The purpose was not to turn engagement into a psychological diagnosis, but to allow the existing Navarasa analytical layer to recognize conversational curiosity that was previously invisible to the narrow vocabulary.
Commit:
477f766

Branch:
v0/fix-navarasa-engagement

16. Session Archetype

A session-scoped archetype was introduced using information from:
- interaction profile
- selection pattern
- trajectory
Possible archetypes include:
- The Curious Cartographer
- The Pattern Keeper
- The Inner Witness
- The Quiet Observer
The archetype is explicitly scoped to the single interaction.
It is not intended to function as a permanent psychological label.
The result is returned by the backend and displayed in the Data Journey.
Local commit:
f31966e

Branch:
v0/session-archetype

